{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01PmvpBmvt1Dmw3BTP3vttZs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All gates green. Here's the summary.\n\n## Done\n\n**Root cause.** `cli-process-report-repair.test.ts` (an Epic-02 file, hash-locked in the red manifest) is the one process-suite test that relied on Vitest's default **5000ms** `testTimeout`. Its `requeue` test spawns several `dist/cli.js` subprocesses; in isolation that's ~3.8s, but under the full `verify-all` suite the spawn latency climbs with CPU contention. Story 1 added two new process-suite files (`cli-process-inspect.test.ts`, `messages-read.test.ts`), bumping the concurrently-running set to 40 files — enough extra contention to push that test to ~5.7s and trip the timeout.\n\n**Fix** (`vitest.config.ts` only — the test file is hash-locked):\n\n```ts\n// Process-suite tests spawn dist/cli.js subprocesses; ... they need headroom\n// past Vitest's 5s default. ... This floor covers the ones that don't —\n// notably the hash-locked cli-process-report-repair — without touching the\n// locked test. Plain verify keeps the tight 5s default ...\n...(includeProcessSuite ? { testTimeout: 30000, hookTimeout: 30000 } : {}),\n```\n\nThis mirrors the existing convention — every *editable* process file already sets explicit per-test timeouts (30s floor; 60s/120s for compaction-heavy legs). Those per-test values override this global, so the heavy legs are untouched. The 30s floor only applies when `LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1`; plain `verify` keeps the tight 5s default so unit tests stay fast and a real hang surfaces quickly.\n\n**Why this doesn't weaken Story 1.** No hash-locked test was edited (the assertions and the focused passing behavior are unchanged — it's purely wall-clock headroom for subprocess spawns), and the config file isn't in the red manifest.\n\n**Verification:**\n- `LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 vitest run test/cli-process-report-repair.test.ts` → 3 passed (focused behavior preserved)\n- `pnpm verify-all` → **40 files / 337 tests passed**; build, typecheck, lint, boundaries all OK\n- `pnpm green-verify` → 300 tests pass + `test-immutability: OK (43 Red-phase files unchanged)` — confirms Story 1's red-manifest immutability is intact"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":888,"cache_read_input_tokens":52659,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":888},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"468b9ce0-fb77-433b-844d-36c8f728df81","uuid":"ce87b046-0434-4001-b126-76a451fbdc4e","request_id":"req_011CbyVaj9ft4gYK2JfHRdLs"}
